    "result_text": "The full suite is green. The three test files are `AcceptanceTest` (the 2 runnable tests), plus `AcceptanceBase` and `AuditLogCapture` support classes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` derivation so that `GET /api/owners/{id}` (and every other owner response) returns the canonical region derived from the city.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/Locality.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility class holding the fixed city-to-region table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) with a pure `fromCity(String)` method that returns the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` for absent/`null` cities. Keeping the table in its own unit avoids bloating the mapper with domain data and makes it reusable.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema, mirroring the existing derived fields (`displayName`, `membershipTier`, etc.). This regenerates `OwnerDto` with the `locality` field.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired one `@Mapping` for `locality` that delegates to `Locality.fromCity(owner.getCity())`, consistent with how the other derived read-only fields are mapped.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` \u2192 `NSW`, `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) pass and the build is green.\n\nNote: I used the fully-qualified class name in the MapStruct `expression` because MapStruct does not carry the mapper interface's imports into the generated `OwnerMapperImpl`.",
